# status: a failing core call (system.get_status) exits 1 with its own RPC
# error before the optional calls run. The blocking upgrade handler proves
# the order: it must never be reached, or the 1s timeout would turn the
# error into a context deadline. No timing is asserted; the error kind is
# exact, which only a core-first implementation produces.

exits 1 glinet-cli -timeout 1s status
! stdout .
stderr '^glinet-cli: system\.get_status: Internal error \(code -32603\)$'

-- handlers.json --
{"fail":["system.get_status"],"block":["upgrade.check_firmware_online"]}
